Function name: `prefix_sum_parallel`  
Parameters:  
- `int* a`: pointer to the input array  
- `size_t n`: total number of elements in the array  
- `size_t block_size`: number of elements per block  

Return type: `void`  

Brief description:  
Executes a **parallel prefix sum** (inclusive scan) on the array `a` using OpenMP and block-wise synchronization. It divides the array into `block_size`-sized chunks and launches each chunk in parallel threads. A shared `flag` array is used for inter-block dependency handling, ensuring that each block waits for the previous one to complete before applying the accumulated result. The total execution time is measured using `omp_get_wtime()` and printed after computation.

code_gens.code:
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <omp.h>

#define N 1024

void prefix_sum_parallel(int* a, size_t n, size_t block_size) {
    double start_time = omp_get_wtime();

    // Initialize flag array with all zeros
    int* flag = (int*)malloc(n * sizeof(int));
    memset(flag, 0, n * sizeof(int));

    // Launch parallel regions for each block
    #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static, block_size)
    for (size_t i = 0; i < n / block_size; i++) {
        size_t start = i * block_size;
        size_t end = std::min(start + block_size, n);

        // Perform local prefix sum within each block
        int sum = 0;
        for (size_t j = start; j < end; j++) {
            sum += a[j];
            a[j] = sum;
        }

        // Update flag array to indicate completion of this block
        flag[start / block_size] = 1;
    }

    // Wait for all blocks to complete
    while (true) {
        int done = true;
        for (size_t i = 0; i < n / block_size; i++) {
            if (!flag[i]) {
                done = false;
                break;
            }
        }
        if (done) {
            break;
        }
        #pragma omp barrier
    }

    free(flag);

    double end_time = omp_get_wtime();
    printf("Total execution time: %.6f seconds\n", end_time - start_time);
}

